1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:05,197
This love in my heart,
it will burn on forever!

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:09,037
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop!

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,177
No matter where you
are, nothing is too far!

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,857
With our everlasting bones,
we'll reach it, we are home!

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:22,637
I'm

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,917
so truly grateful!

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,800
I ran into you on that day so long ago!

8
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,397
We laughed every moment
with tears in our eyes!

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,860
Till we knew we weren't alone!

10
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:41,840
The blowing wind came in
and joined us on our way!

11
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,097
And with it I know we'll rise!

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,797
We'll be flying up high!

13
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,920
Why, tell me why are you giving up?

14
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,160
Why, tell me why you want to fight alone?

15
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,620
Hey, what kind of future
do you think you have?

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,197
Your dream is already in your hands.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,937
This love in my heart,
it will burn off forever.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,757
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,897
I don't matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

20
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,457
With our everlasting
plans, we'll reach it.

21
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:20,537
We are home from the horizon,
out on the edge of the world.

22
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,477
If there is a place that
I want to take you to?

23
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,897
Let's head for it then!

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,420
But as for the way, we already know.

25
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,640
We promised it long ago.

26
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,317
You scream by your voice.

27
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,237
That can't break through the silence.

28
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,817
Feeling defeated.

29
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,037
It crushes your helpless heart.

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,697
I've got your back, I swear.

31
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,177
I'll always be here.

32
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:58,020
Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

33
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,880
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,917
Let's find the answer together.

35
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,577
I'm telling you in our path.

36
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,617
I trust that it will lead us.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,517
To another sea untarded.

38
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,397
Cause now we are home.

39
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,127
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

40
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,197
There is a place that
I want to take you to.

41
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,717
Let's head for it then.

42
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,240
But after the wave, we already know.

43
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,380
We promised it long ago.

44
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,960
Chop Chop Chop Chop.

45
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:37,220
Chop Chop Chop Chop.

46
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:57,557
By the way, do you ever read the W .E .J.?

47
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,960
The World Economic Journal?

48
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,260
It's a major paper, Lili.

49
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,940
Everyone knows it.

50
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,640
They used to run this awesome comic strip.

51
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,194
It was called Saru, Warrior of the Sea.

52
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:12,241
Had a giant robot and everything.

53
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:15,400
I wouldn't miss it for my life, Lili.

54
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,497
Saru was this hero who
could walk on water.

55
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:21,937
He had a transforming robot
and a little Skull pal, too.

56
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:27,320
And the bad guys, the evil armies of Germa
double six, enemies to all marines, Lili.

57
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,537
People all over the world love that comic.

58
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:33,817
I know it looks like a kid's story on
the surface, but from what I heard,

59
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:38,177
it was actually based on true reports
from the big shot Navy heroes, Lili.

60
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,997
So it's pretty much propaganda,

61
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:43,657
teaching the little kiddies that the Navy
is always right and always wins the day,

62
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:44,880
Lili. Lo, lo, lo.

63
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:49,160
So why would a guy like me read
a comic like that, you ask?

64
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:50,615
Why for the villains!

65
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,560
For Germa double six!

66
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:58,017
Their armies used every dirty trick in
the book to try and pull one over on Saru.

67
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:00,940
They were a role model
for outlaws like me.

68
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:04,970
Anyway,

69
00:04:05,053 --> 00:04:07,477
I get that Germa has to lose
for the sake of the story,

70
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,197
but I always cheered for them.

71
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,680
You guys are the best!

72
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:13,637
Don't tell me that!

73
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:17,937
I've got nothing to do
with them, you know.

74
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:21,157
I'm telling you as a fan in fact I could

75
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,097
hardly wait to meet the
rest of your family.

76
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,097
Little then fanboy over them

77
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:31,537
instead—are you

78
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:32,477
gonna open or not?

79
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,390
So

80
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:48,557
as I was just saying, would
you stop following me?

81
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,337
This is my room, you weirdo.

82
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:54,497
It's supposed to be my room
too, so why am I in a cage?

83
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:56,557
I am a genius scientist.

84
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:59,257
I deserve better treatment than this.

85
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,837
You've been crying about
this all day, Lili.

86
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:07,257
Listen, we were told to
capture you, not pamper you.

87
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:11,117
But Sanji here—he's the
groom that's gonna bring the

88
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:14,237
Vinsmoke family and the
Charlotte family together as one.

89
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:18,257
So you may be a genius,
but he's still worth more.

90
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,170
worth more

91
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,917
Yeah, I'm not getting married.

92
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,260
I told you get the hell out of here.

93
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,780
What did you just say?

94
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:29,140
Ain't nobody disrespects my boy Vito.

95
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,717
Now apologize for your dead meat!

96
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,340
He didn't hurt my feelings at all.

97
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,757
I mean thanks for
sticking up for me buddy.

98
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,917
Yeah, but he was just playing around

99
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,220
No, I was serious.

100
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:49,940
Both of you, get the hell out
of my room right now. Again?

101
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,180
I heard that.

102
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,880
Oh, it is on now!

103
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,720
Hey, you don't do it!

104
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:57,460
Insult me, but don't insult my friends.

105
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,500
I'll kill you!

106
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,557
We're trying to be pals here.

107
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,700
Let it go, Lili.

108
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:03,570
Don't bother.

109
00:06:03,653 --> 00:06:04,540
I hate your guts.

110
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:08,117
And if you don't leave, I've
got more insults for you.

111
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,557
You son of a...

112
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:11,780
Got it!

113
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,020
What the hell are you trying to pull?

114
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,480
I'm sorry, ma 'am.

115
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:45,978
Kaido, you do realize that he's one
of the Vinsmoke family, don't you?

116
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:51,660
If you lay so much as a finger on him,
then my veggie's head is gonna roll.

117
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,840
Do you understand me? Ha!

118
00:06:57,620 --> 00:07:01,857
Though while we're at it, maybe I should
lop your head off first, you dumb-o.

119
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:02,920
Get out of here!

120
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,977
I'll be nice from now on, I promise!

121
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:05,890
I promise!

122
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,300
Hey, are you...

123
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:10,960
I'm sorry, ma 'am.

124
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,317
It won't happen again.

125
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,697
With punishment, there's
no dinner for you tonight.

126
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:16,520
Please, anything but that!

127
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,980
Yo, Lili, sorry to bother you.

128
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:25,817
We can talk about Janet later, Lili.

129
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,160
Not happening.

130
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:38,500
I know that face.

131
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,720
But I can't remember where.

132
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,017
Alright, I was wrong.

133
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:59,837
I'm gonna die after all.

134
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,437
It's so hot.

135
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,977
I might melt before I starve.

136
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:07,677
I want Saji back on the show.

137
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:10,660
I just need some ice cream.

138
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,900
I wish I could take off my fur.

139
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:22,260
It's not helping right now.

140
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:23,880
I know the feeling.

141
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,619
Minx have a low tolerance for heat.

142
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:31,300
If I can't cool off soon, I fear
I'm going to become a mummy.

143
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,000
Wait, a mummy?

144
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:34,860
Hold on a second.

145
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:36,780
That's a big deal.

146
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,137
Hey, Nami.

147
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:41,632
If I become a mommy, that would
be like an upgrade for me.

148
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,780
I don't care.

149
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:46,920
If I had a fancy sarcophagus,
then could I see your panties?

150
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,360
I wish I had the strength to slap you.

151
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:53,740
Mommy, I'm hungry and
it's hot and I'm tired.

152
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,740
I need some nutrition.

153
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,980
We've had such bad luck.

154
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,740
It's been too stormy
for us to fish at all.

155
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,800
Now the sun's killing us.

156
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:06,517
I know it's hot, but please catch
something while we still have clear skies.

157
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:10,660
Otherwise, we'll all starve to
death before we even get there.

158
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,440
Oh, team food!

159
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:16,560
We're giving it our best, but, uh...

160
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:24,500
It's actually so hot that
the water is boiling.

161
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:25,930
What?

162
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:29,600
So, uh, that's a no on the fish, then?

163
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,380
What should we do?

164
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,080
Huh?

165
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:37,320
Emergency rations.

166
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:39,328
Don't look at me like that!

167
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,880
Wolf! Pull! Quick!

168
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:51,597
It's huge!

169
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,510
It's huge!

170
00:09:52,593 --> 00:09:53,780
I don't want you...

171
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,320
Freddy, help!

172
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:15,140
I'm all cheering for you.

173
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,197
Come on, Luffy, keep fighting!

174
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:21,480
So, we might not die?

175
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:34,280
I got you, Fischity!

176
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:36,480
You did it!

177
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:38,630
Finally!

178
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,360
Yeah, that should be quite the feast.

179
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:44,120
Let's eat!

180
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,220
You're going in my belly!

181
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,960
Yeah, that color is a bad sign.

182
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,640
Might be poisonous.

183
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:00,257
It's a fish that eats food!

184
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:02,157
You don't know what you're talking about!

185
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,475
Just wait one second.

186
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:05,699
I can look it up before we cook it.

187
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:12,557
Not with the saucy ladies already.

188
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,520
I want an encyclopedia of fish!

189
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:16,570
Got it!

190
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,620
Okay. Let's see.

191
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:23,460
Not this one. Oh, come on. Please.

192
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:24,870
Yes!

193
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,398
You can't eat the skin of that fish!

194
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:28,830
It's poisonous!

195
00:11:28,913 --> 00:11:29,976
Extremely poisonous!

196
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:32,057
Sanji made a note about it in here!

197
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,620
Wow, the skin's so good!

198
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,837
I know that you're hungry,
but wait for me to grill it!

199
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:41,120
Here, Kara, you should try
some, too! I don't know.

200
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,480
It's awfully slimy. Luffy!

201
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,700
Okay, dinner's served!

202
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:53,960
Why, that's music to my
ears! I'm famished. Eat out!

203
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,240
Mmm, it's so good!

204
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,286
You're an awesome cook, Nami!

205
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:01,140
Oh, the tears, they won't stop!

206
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:03,580
I feel so alive! Thank you!

207
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:04,920
Such joy!

208
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:09,760
I just followed Sanji's
recipe, so don't thank me!

209
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:16,180
Chopper, eat something
before you pass out!

210
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,300
Here, take it.

211
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,740
Boobie's doing bad.

212
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,880
I'm afraid he's gonna die.

213
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:29,480
I'm so, so cold, Chopper. Help me.

214
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,540
Crying isn't gonna save him.

215
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:35,957
Have some fish to get
that brain working again,

216
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:38,457
and I know you'll come up
with a plan to fix this.

217
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,740
Now here, eat up.

218
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:46,720
But even if I can't stop
crying, it's no use.

219
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:50,180
I already used up all of our antidotes.

220
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:56,510
Yum.

221
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,740
We gotta find an island, Nami.

222
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,800
I don't want him to die.

223
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,660
Is that food?

224
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:16,750
Damn it.

225
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:19,120
Why isn't it easier to find land?

226
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:23,340
I looked at Sanji's notes myself,
and according to his book,

227
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:25,957
the poison from the skin
should kill you right away.

228
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:26,870
Uh-huh.

229
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,010
Yeah.

230
00:13:28,093 --> 00:13:29,877
But he didn't react at all till now.

231
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:32,157
And even though he's
sick, he's still not dead.

232
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:34,997
Maybe we should have more
faith in Luffy's vitality.

233
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,940
I guess, but look at him.

234
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:41,820
Yum.

235
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:45,360
Are you, Tia, gonna die?

236
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:50,540
The river, it's so beautiful.

237
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,245
Guys, he's at the river stand!

238
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:59,120
We're about to enter Mama's
territory any moment now. Huh?

239
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,910
First,

240
00:14:03,993 --> 00:14:05,977
we'll run into a bunch
of smaller islands with

241
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:08,677
the defense network
surrounding Whole Cake Island.

242
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:13,137
Since there's no reason for Blackleg and
his little entourage to get held up there,

243
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:16,044
he's probably reached
Whole Cake Island already.

244
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:27,300
No matter what, don't lower your guard.

245
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,433
I'll go keep a lookout.

246
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:34,244
I had planned to stop at
the first island ahead.

247
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:36,265
We can find an antidote there.

248
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,520
What the?

249
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,940
It was hot and now it's snowing?

250
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,430
Pretty.

251
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,220
Hold on.

252
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,461
That's not snow.

253
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,680
Are those sugar clouds? Yep.

254
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:54,880
We call this a cotton candy flurry.

255
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,680
Cotton candy!

256
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:02,800
What are you doing here?

257
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:05,930
Yummy!

258
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,520
What's that?

259
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,020
We're giving a call? Not exactly.

260
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,577
What you're hearing is a warning signal.

261
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,020
That is to say,

262
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:33,577
We've entered Mama's territory, and
her troops are going to know about it.

263
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:34,880
I'm getting it!

264
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:37,257
Hider, disguise yourselves as something!

265
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:39,440
I'm trying to help you! Yeah!

266
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:43,200
Are you ignoring me?

267
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:50,000
I see something! Pec-Oms!

268
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,480
It's a ship!

269
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,191
It's coming right for us!

270
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:57,190
What?

271
00:15:57,273 --> 00:15:59,680
How did they get here so fast?

272
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:01,900
Who is they?

273
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:03,377
It's called the Tart.

274
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:05,460
They're one of Mama's scout ships.

275
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,330
Great.

276
00:16:07,413 --> 00:16:09,038
I can't make it out through the fog.

277
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:10,280
What should we do?

278
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:11,477
You go hide.

279
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,325
I'll handle this mess somehow.

280
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,580
Works for me. This is bad.

281
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:18,272
I think Ubi's condition is getting worse.

282
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,220
The poison is spreading.

283
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:24,597
I don't know if he can hold on much
longer without some kind of treatment.

284
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:27,157
Do you think they'll have
something on the scout ship?

285
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:30,520
Alas, but you've got to
hide right now! Okay!

286
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:33,680
Come on, Chopper, double time!

287
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,720
Oh, my God.

288
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,240
I'm in there.

289
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:36,620
Is that a transponder, snail?

290
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,060
It's huge!

291
00:17:38,940 --> 00:17:41,220
I wonder what that number could mean.

292
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:43,560
Sixty-six.

293
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,340
This is Germa.

294
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,504
Is that Straw Hat Luffy's ship?

295
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:54,860
Just don't look, it's Germa Double Six!

296
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,300
So it's not Big Mom after all.

297
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,340
They call Germa Double Six the warmongers.

298
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:05,511
What business do you have in these waters?

299
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,800
Answer, quickly!

300
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,665
We're about to hit their ship!

301
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:11,897
We're on the sails!

302
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:12,810
Hurry!

303
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:17,200
Lucy, I'll be back.

304
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,900
Seems we avoided a crash, at least.

305
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:54,830
Sanji!

306
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,790
Sanji!

307
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:01,080
That curly eyebrow! No!

308
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:04,200
It must be him! What? Really? We did it?

309
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:06,270
Sanji!

310
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,120
I can't believe we found you!

311
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:12,800
And I can't believe that
we found Sanji so quickly!

312
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:14,774
Quite the coincidence.

313
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,460
Hey, Sanji, we have a problem!

314
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:24,348
Luffy ate some poisoned
fish and he's dying!

315
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:27,664
Do you have an antidote
on that big ship, maybe?

316
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:28,880
It's urgent!

317
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:32,960
Wait, can't you hear me? Sanji!

318
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,960
You got the wrong guy.

319
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:42,440
Well, I guess we might look alike.

320
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,500
But my name is Yonji.

321
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:52,170
Yonji?

322
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,578
But he's got curly eyebrows, though.

323
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:57,677
If he's not Sanji, then
who in the heck's Yonji?

324
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:02,220
My relationship with your associate
Sanji is a highly classified matter.

325
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:05,641
It's a secret that I'll
take to the grave with me.

326
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,978
That's his younger brother for sure.

327
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:12,760
Wonder who else is in his family.

328
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,717
How do you know they're related?

329
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:15,682
I don't get it.

330
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:18,670
Cutie!

331
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:22,720
Are you saying that, Sanji?

332
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,320
Yonji, sir.

333
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:29,497
Not to interrupt, but I don't think
we'll find Master Sanji on that ship.

334
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:32,286
It seems we missed each
other on the way here.

335
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,840
So it would appear.

336
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,394
Let's pull back, then.

337
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,051
This was a waste of time.

338
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,700
Hey, come back! Sanji!

339
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,240
I'm Yonji!

340
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,860
Oh, no! Luffy!

341
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,360
He's developing a rash.

342
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,069
He can't fight it anymore.

343
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:57,240
I know Luffy has strong antibodies, so
this poison must be really powerful.

344
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,300
Stay with us, please.

345
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:07,257
It's just a poison from
a stupid fish, right?

346
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:09,817
If you're going to be king of
the pirates, then fight back.

347
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:10,730
She's right.

348
00:21:10,813 --> 00:21:11,757
You can't die now.

349
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:12,880
Don't give up.

350
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,560
You gotta help us.

351
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:18,717
We used all of our antidotes on him, but
his condition just keeps getting worse.

352
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:20,624
You must have something, right?

353
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:24,897
I'm begging you!

354
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:27,757
If nothing else, can you
do it for Sanji at least?

355
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:30,016
Don't let your brother's captain die!

356
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,220
Sorry, guys.

357
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:38,600
I'm not into the whole saving lives thing.

358
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:44,660
But if you want that medicine so
bad, why don't you take it from us?

359
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:47,400
You guys are pirates, aren't you?

360
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:51,597
He only has Sanji's bad parts
and none of the good ones!

361
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,997
He's a playboy jerk!

362
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:55,100
Why are you, Tia, being so cruel?

363
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,420
Just say the word and he's dead.

364
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:01,700
Yunji. Huh?

365
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,940
Stop being so stinging, will you?

366
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:12,380
Don't you, sir!

367
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,720
What is going on?

368
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:21,290
Luffy!

369
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:25,260
Lady Major!

370
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:31,480
Hang in there!

371
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:35,100
Don't die!

372
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:39,840
Luffy! No!

373
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:54,520
Who are you, Pia? An enemy?

374
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:11,040
Do forgive him.

375
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,900
He's rather heartless.

376
00:23:14,380 --> 00:23:16,000
A creep, too.

377
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:18,400
But never mind, my little brother.

378
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:20,173
I'll set this straight.

379
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,880
Your little brother?

380
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:31,200
Are you related to Sanji?

381
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,880
She's got curly eyebrows, too!

382
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,880
She's lovely!

383
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,400
Thank you!

384
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:55,100
He flies? Damn it!

385
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:58,057
What were you thinking
humiliating me like that?

386
00:23:58,140 --> 00:24:00,669
Buffoon, you should be
ashamed of yourself.

387
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:05,260
Oh, I wonder how he's floating.

388
00:24:05,740 --> 00:24:07,580
It's technology. Huh?

389
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:10,417
They're powerful, don't get me wrong.

390
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:13,217
but the strength of
German double six is the

391
00:24:13,300 --> 00:24:16,257
strength of science you
might call them a scientific

392
00:24:16,340 --> 00:24:21,817
fighting squad that's
why mama's interested

393
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:25,757
she wants that technology

394
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:29,857
for herself back homes

395
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:34,377
that name rings a bell
if I recall Vinsmoke was

396
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:40,317
the name of a royal
family many years ago they

397
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:42,997
conquered the north blue
i believe and they did

398
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:45,920
so with an overwhelming
show of military might

399
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:50,857
royalty like vivi or like neptune's family

400
00:24:50,940 --> 00:24:54,997
so they're actually
really famous that's right

401
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:59,217
their name was synonymous
with evil in fact

402
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:02,740
in a comic strip they
were used as villains i'm

403
00:25:03,960 --> 00:25:04,790
impressed.

404
00:25:04,873 --> 00:25:06,017
You're a regular historian.

405
00:25:06,100 --> 00:25:07,957
I've been alive for a long time.

406
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:09,040
And dead as well.

407
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:13,400
You see, it's not just a story.

408
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:17,177
For even still, we are royalty.

409
00:25:17,260 --> 00:25:19,120
Germa is a nation without soil.

410
00:25:19,420 --> 00:25:24,302
We own no territory, but we are given the
right to attend the reverie all the same.

411
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:27,870
I see.

412
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:29,477
Then I beg your pardon.

413
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:32,360
May I see your royal panties?

414
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:33,860
Most honored lady?

415
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,660
Stop it!

416
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:47,058
Now, if you don't mind, I'll
be taking that from him.

417
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:53,706
I'm going to guess he ate the skin of an
armored stonefish from the boiling sea.

418
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:55,800
Yeah, but how did you know?

419
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:59,120
This poison has very particular effects.

420
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:02,440
He's quite the glutton.

421
00:26:02,740 --> 00:26:04,617
Even a giant wouldn't survive this.

422
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:05,530
What?

423
00:26:05,613 --> 00:26:06,760
We can't save him?

424
00:26:07,100 --> 00:26:09,280
But there has to be some way!

425
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:11,940
I fail!

426
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,200
I'm the worst doctor in the world!

427
00:26:15,700 --> 00:26:17,600
But this is good.

428
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:18,700
You're lucky.

429
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:20,520
It's my favorite.

430
00:26:22,300 --> 00:26:24,520
This poison is the best.

431
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,780
What are you doing?

432
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:32,540
Down the hatch.

433
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:42,400
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

434
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:45,900
If you suck out that
poison, you'll die for sure!

435
00:26:46,460 --> 00:26:48,400
Oh, I'm so jealous!

436
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:51,780
If only I could trade places with him!

437
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:57,160
Though, alas, my lips are long gone!

438
00:27:13,140 --> 00:27:15,820
The rash is transferring?

439
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:48,760
There's no more rash.

440
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:49,960
It's all gone.

441
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:52,040
You sucked it out.

442
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:53,360
Are you okay?

443
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:58,200
Never felt better,
because I'm Poison Pink.

444
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:01,940
Is that a code name?

445
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:10,260
Mm-hmm, delicious. Whoa!

446
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,360
Whoa, what happened?

447
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:25,920
Bluefeet!

448
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:27,440
You're okay!

449
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:30,460
I was so scared!

450
00:28:30,820 --> 00:28:32,137
I thought you had got her for sure!

451
00:28:32,220 --> 00:28:33,460
I'm so happy!

452
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:35,510
Luffy!

453
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:40,860
Wait, did I fall asleep while
I was eating that giant fish?

454
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:44,720
The skin part was really
good! Is there any left? No!

455
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,118
You don't remember?

456
00:28:50,380 --> 00:28:51,210
Soji!

457
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:52,760
That's a woman!

458
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:54,760
Actually, you're right.

459
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,980
Luffy, she's the person
who just saved your life.

460
00:28:59,340 --> 00:29:00,170
Huh?

461
00:29:00,253 --> 00:29:01,083
Thanks, lady.

462
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:02,210
She what?

463
00:29:05,260 --> 00:29:07,960
So that's the infamous Straw Hat Luffy.

464
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:10,220
I see. Cool.

465
00:29:10,580 --> 00:29:12,698
I never knew Sanji had a big sister.

466
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:14,410
Yes.

467
00:29:14,493 --> 00:29:15,323
That's right.

468
00:29:15,406 --> 00:29:17,620
Sanji is a Vinsmoke like us.

469
00:29:19,420 --> 00:29:21,980
He was separated from
us when he was young.

470
00:29:22,520 --> 00:29:25,344
Our father's been searching
for him for a while.

471
00:29:26,140 --> 00:29:30,199
About two years ago, when Sanji's
wanted poster was first circulated,

472
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:34,913
My father personally requested that
the Navy make catching him a priority.

473
00:29:36,340 --> 00:29:40,380
Sadly, they pursued a man
named Devil by mistake.

474
00:29:41,020 --> 00:29:41,850
Devil?

475
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:47,932
He's the guy from the Flying Fish Riders.

476
00:29:48,100 --> 00:29:50,629
We met him right before
we went to Sabaody.

477
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:55,060
Ah, Sanji was not a
fan of that whole mess.

478
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:59,837
It wasn't until recently that the
government finally ironed things out.

479
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:02,397
When your crew made
your surprise comeback,

480
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:05,177
they captured an image of
Sanji during the chaos.

481
00:30:05,260 --> 00:30:08,097
Afterwards, they gave us a
call to share the good news.

482
00:30:08,180 --> 00:30:11,474
Of course, our father raised
Sanji's bounty immediately.

483
00:30:11,740 --> 00:30:15,000
As for the dead or
alive, that was no good.

484
00:30:15,620 --> 00:30:19,660
So it was changed to
say only alive instead.

485
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:21,280
So that's why.

486
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:25,596
We knew there was something behind
that, but we couldn't figure it out.

487
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:32,117
Okay so where's Sanji right now?

488
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:37,997
Can't say he could be with Big Mom
or he could be with our father.

489
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:43,580
We thought we might catch him on
the way, but we were too late.

490
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:51,557
Well we'll see him at the tea party,
and that's the important part!

491
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:55,540
They won't be long now,
and I even got to meet you?

492
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:01,100
You took good care of Sanji for that.

493
00:31:01,280 --> 00:31:02,110
I'm grateful

494
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,720
Sanji sister

495
00:31:12,700 --> 00:31:16,940
Thanks for saving my
life for real, but still

496
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,500
We're taking Sanjuvac.

497
00:31:20,660 --> 00:31:23,080
He's my Gourmet, my friend.

498
00:31:49,540 --> 00:31:51,840
I won't give up on him!

499
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:58,740
So, dumb.

500
00:31:59,140 --> 00:32:00,900
Don't save your enemy's life.

501
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:03,920
Hey, you!

502
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:07,242
You're Peckham's from the
Big Mom Pirates, right?

503
00:32:07,580 --> 00:32:11,286
So what the hell are you doing
hanging out with the Straw Hats?

504
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:15,437
I have my reasons, and
that's all I'm gonna say.

505
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:19,120
I got no obligation to
explain it to you get out

506
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:24,017
Things might be different after this
wedding ceremony, but right now.

507
00:32:24,100 --> 00:32:25,737
You're just some random guy.

508
00:32:25,820 --> 00:32:27,540
I can't argue with that

509
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:36,877
For the time being, at least now,
pretend this meeting never happened.

510
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:40,517
Good call—our mistake for
butting in, if you ask me.

511
00:32:40,600 --> 00:32:43,477
We don't want to cause any trouble
and put the wedding in jeopardy.

512
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:44,390
jeopardy

513
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:48,860
I'd recommend you tread lightly as well.

514
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,100
You do have some sense! Get on!

515
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:53,460
Raise the anchor. Let's move.

516
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:00,350
Good luck.

517
00:33:00,433 --> 00:33:01,440
I'll be seeing you.

518
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:33,540
They ran into Germa, but it
seems they avoided a fight.

519
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:36,984
Yeah, I'm sure it's their ship.

520
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:40,179
I can confirm that Straw
Hat Luffy is on board, too.

521
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:43,510
What's next?

522
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:46,900
Jinbei...
